  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical concave mirrors each of focal length $f$ are facing each other as shown in the schematic diagram. The focal length $f$ is much larger than the size of the mirrors. A glass slab of thickness $t$ and refractive index $n_0$ is kept equidistant from the mirrors and perpendicular to their common principal axis. A monochromatic point light source $S$ is embedded at the center of the slab on the principal axis, as shown in the schematic diagram. For the image to be formed on $S$ itself, which of the following distances between the two mirrors is/are correct:\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/9u3Ryufz01wkAhJzx6epAkQlygdD24jOmx-TEP6TMLU.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7A4f2",
      "text": "$4 f+\\left(1-\\frac{1}{n_0}\\right) t$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "iEyrb",
      "text": "$2 f+\\left(1-\\frac{1}{n_0}\\right) t$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zjWgO",
      "text": "$4 f+\\left(n_0-1\\right) t$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bwcMS",
      "text": "$2 f+\\left(n_0-1\\right) t$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/6LUfEWL638X9V5UPRUBCj8iI6kxtLGdpltCTHbi90i4.original.fullsize.png\"><br>$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{S-t}{2}+\\frac{t}{2 n_0}=2 f \\\\ & S+t\\left(\\frac{1}{n_0}-1\\right)=4 f \\\\ & S=4 f+\\left(1-\\frac{1}{n_0}\\right) t\\end{aligned}$\nAlso\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{\\mathrm{S}-\\mathrm{t}}{2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{t}}{2 \\mathrm{n}_0}=\\mathrm{f} \\\\ & \\mathrm{S}=2 \\mathrm{f}+\\left(1-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_0}\\right) \\mathrm{t}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
